x?.let { } ->is a functional null-safe scope function that executes only when the value is non-null and allows chaining.
    Executes the block only if x is not null
    Inside the block, x is available as non-null
    Uses safe call operator (?.)

if (x != null) ->is a traditional null check with smart casting, better suited for complex logic.
    Traditional null check
    Smart cast inside block

