ABOUT HAL(Hardware Abstraction Layer)
    ->Android HAL acts as a bridge between the Android framework (Java APIs) and the low-level Linux kernel (device drivers).
    ->Android HAL provides standard interfaces for hardware components so the Android framework can access hardware like:
        | Hardware   | Android Framework API |
        | ---------- | --------------------- |
        | Camera     | camera2             |
        | Audio      | AudioManager        |
        | Bluetooth  | android.bluetooth   |
        | WiFi       | android.net.wifi    |
        | Sensors    | SensorManager       |
        | GPS        | LocationManager     |
        | NFC        | android.nfc         |
        | Biometrics | BiometricPrompt     |
        | Vibrator   | Vibrator            |
        | USB        | UsbManager          |
        | Display    | DisplayManager      |
        | Telephony  | TelephonyManager    |
        | Storage    | StorageManager      |
        | Battery    | BatteryManager      |
        | Vehicle    | android.car         |

    ->How does an Android app access hardware?
         Android Applications
                 ↓
         Android Framework (CameraManager, BluetoothManager, etc.)
                 ↓
         Native System Services
                 ↓
         HAL (Hardware Abstraction Layer)
                 ↓
         Linux Kernel Drivers
                 ↓
         Hardware
    -Example:
        Camera App
           ↓
        CameraManager API
           ↓
        Camera Service
           ↓
        Camera HAL
           ↓
        Camera Driver
           ↓
        Camera Hardware

    -Why HAL Exists
        Without HAL:
        ✔ Android framework must support every hardware driver separately
        ✔ Huge complexity
        ✔ Poor portability

        With HAL:
        ✔ Hardware vendors implement their own HAL
        ✔ Android framework remains unchanged
        ✔ Device manufacturers can customize hardware

        Example – Camera HAL When an app takes a picture:
            App calls: CameraManager.openCamera()
            Framework sends request to: Camera Service
            Camera Service calls: Camera HAL
            HAL communicates with: Linux camera driver
            Driver controls: Camera hardware

    ->Types of HAL
        1️⃣ Legacy HAL (Pre-Treble HAL)
        2️⃣ HIDL HAL (Binderized HAL) (Hardware Interface Definition Language)
        3️⃣ AIDL HAL (Modern HAL) (Android Interface Definition Language)

        | Feature            | Legacy HAL          | HIDL HAL         | AIDL HAL         |
        | ------------------ | ------------------- | ---------------- | ---------------- |
        | Android Version    | < Android 8         | Android 8+       | Android 11+      |
        | Communication      | Direct library call | Binder IPC       | Binder IPC       |
        | Interface Language | C/C++               | HIDL             | AIDL             |
        | Process            | Same process        | Separate process | Separate process |
        | Treble Support     | ❌                  | ✅              | ✅               |

        SensorHAL Evolution:
        OLD (Pre-Treble)    :Framework → HAL Library → Driver
                            App → Framework → System Service → Legacy HAL (C/C++ library) → Linux Driver → Hardware

        TREBLE (Android 8+) :Framework → Binder → HIDL HAL → Driver
                            App → Framework → System Service → Binder IPC → HIDL Interface → HAL Service (Vendor) → Driver → Hardware

        MODERN (Android 11+):Framework → Binder → AIDL HAL → Driver
                            App → Framework → System Service → Binder IPC → AIDL Interface → HAL Service → Driver → Hardware


    ->Where HAL Code Exists
        In Android source tree:  /hardware/
        Example:
          hardware/interfaces/camera/
          hardware/interfaces/bluetooth/
          hardware/interfaces/audio/

        Vendor implementations: /vendor/<company>/hardware/
        Example: vendor/qcom/camera/

    ->Real Devices Example
      If Samsung builds a phone:
          Samsung writes its own Camera HAL
          Android framework still uses the same Camera API
      So Android does not care about Samsung camera hardware implementation.

    ->HAL vs Drivers
       | Layer        | Responsibility                 |
       | ------------ | ------------------------------ |
       | HAL          | Standard interface for Android |
       | Linux Driver | Direct hardware control        |
       | Hardware     | Physical device                |

       Example:
           Android Camera API
                  ↓
           Camera HAL
                  ↓
           Linux Camera Driver
                  ↓
           Image Sensor

    ->How HAL Works
        1 Android Applications
             ↓
        2 Android Framework (Java API)
             ↓
        3 System Service (Native / system_server)
             ↓
        4 Binder IPC
             ↓
        5 HAL Interface
             ↓
        6 HAL Implementation (Vendor)
             ↓
        7 Linux Kernel Driver
             ↓
        8 Hardware


